From: Primoz Ajdisek <bigpod@bigpod.si>
Subject: [PATCH] build: exclude node-pty Linux prebuilds from Linux payloads

node-pty now ships Linux prebuilds for both architectures. The Linux desktop
build rebuilds node-pty into build/Release, so these are unused. Bundling them
makes native package dependency scanners try to resolve a foreign ABI.
---
 scripts/build-desktop-artifact.ts | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/build-desktop-artifact.ts b/scripts/build-desktop-artifact.ts
--- a/scripts/build-desktop-artifact.ts
+++ b/scripts/build-desktop-artifact.ts
@@ -972,6 +972,7 @@
-// Linux builds node-pty from source, so every prebuild in the package is for
-// another platform (58 MB of it Windows debug symbols).
+// Linux builds node-pty from source into build/Release. Exclude all prebuilds,
+// including Linux binaries for other architectures.
 export const LINUX_FILE_EXCLUSIONS = [
   ...MAC_FILE_EXCLUSIONS,
   "!**/node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/darwin-*/**/*",
+  "!**/node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/linux-*/**/*",
 ] as const;
